237
00:23:20,622 --> 00:23:31,106
[SPEAKER_04]: Regardless of whether or not they feel violent, painful, sharp, severe, acute feelings, they are incapable of knowledge and vision of supreme awakening.

238
00:23:31,826 --> 00:23:33,547
[SPEAKER_04]: This was the first simile that occurred to me.

239
00:23:33,647 --> 00:23:34,988
[SPEAKER_04]: Then, a second simile occurred to me.

240
00:23:35,708 --> 00:23:40,110
[SPEAKER_04]: Suppose there was a green sappy log and it was lying on dry land, far from the water.

241
00:23:40,990 --> 00:23:44,712
[SPEAKER_04]: Then, a man comes along with an upper fire stick, thinking to light a fire and produce heat.

242
00:23:45,292 --> 00:23:46,413
[SPEAKER_04]: What do you think, Aggivessana?

243
00:23:46,453 --> 00:23:53,456
[SPEAKER_04]: By drilling the stick against that green sappy log on dry land, far from water, could they light a fire and produce heat?

244
00:23:53,536 --> 00:23:54,417
[SPEAKER_04]: No, Master Gautama.

245
00:23:54,497 --> 00:23:54,897
[SPEAKER_04]: Why not?

246
00:23:55,931 --> 00:24:01,794
[SPEAKER_04]: Because it's still a green, sappy log, despite the fact that it's lying on dry land, far from water.

247
00:24:02,294 --> 00:24:04,455
[SPEAKER_04]: That person will eventually get weary and frustrated.

248
00:24:05,016 --> 00:24:16,741
[SPEAKER_04]: In the same way, there are ascetics and brahmins who do live withdrawn in body and mind from sensuality, but they haven't internally given up and allay desire, affection, infatuation, thirst and burning for sensuality.

249
00:24:17,362 --> 00:24:25,086
[SPEAKER_04]: Regardless of whether or not they feel violent, painful, sharp, severe, acute feelings, they are incapable of knowledge and vision of supreme awakening.

250
00:24:25,806 --> 00:24:27,447
[SPEAKER_04]: This was the second simile that occurred to me.

251
00:24:28,027 --> 00:24:29,468
[SPEAKER_04]: Then, a third simile occurred to me.

252
00:24:29,548 --> 00:24:34,632
[SPEAKER_04]: Suppose there was a dried-up, withered log, and it was lying on dry land, far from the water.

253
00:24:35,832 --> 00:24:38,054
[SPEAKER_04]: Then, the man comes along, trying to light the fire stick.

254
00:24:38,814 --> 00:24:44,498
[SPEAKER_04]: By drilling the stick against that dried-up, withered log on dry land, far from water, could they light a fire and produce heat?

255
00:24:45,038 --> 00:24:46,039
[SPEAKER_04]: Yes, Master Gautama.

256
00:24:46,059 --> 00:24:46,519
[SPEAKER_04]: Why is that?

257
00:24:47,020 --> 00:24:50,222
[SPEAKER_04]: Because it's a dried-up, withered log, and it's drying on dry land.

258
00:24:51,082 --> 00:24:51,702
[SPEAKER_04]: Far from water.

259
00:24:51,722 --> 00:24:52,003
[SPEAKER_04]: So...

