00:32:12,240 --> 00:32:12,980
[SPEAKER_04]: Well, exactly.

334
00:32:13,020 --> 00:32:17,742
[SPEAKER_04]: So, basically, what I'm trying to say is, it's a way of trying to overcompensate.

335
00:32:18,266 --> 00:32:18,866
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, exactly.

336
00:32:18,886 --> 00:32:19,406
[SPEAKER_03]: That's what I'm saying.

337
00:32:19,426 --> 00:32:29,910
